    "result_text": "The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and both its tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the Owner resource.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getOwnerSegment()`:\n```java\npublic String getOwnerSegment() {\n    String tier = getMembershipLevel() >= 3 ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n    String area = REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey(getLocality()) ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n    return tier + \"_\" + area;\n}\n```\n- **TIER** is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD` \u2014 reusing the existing `getMembershipLevel()` accessor.\n- **AREA** is `METRO` when the owner's `locality` is a known region, else `REGIONAL`. I reused the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (keyed exactly by `NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`) as the single source of known regions, and read `getLocality()` rather than re-deriving a region \u2014 consistent with the codebase's \"single region identity\" convention.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, matching the style of the sibling derived fields (`locality`, `timezone`, `ageBand`). This drives the generated `OwnerDto`, which MapStruct auto-maps from the new getter by name.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown region) pass, and the full build is green.",
